Z||000000||Adrift||10-22-2001||06:52 PM||||I have a pair of 6 1/2's and 6 x 9's. <BR>Here's what I'm currently thinking:<BR> <BR>6 1/2"' in the door, with their tweeters mounted on the plastic lining the windshield (At ear level)<P>6 x 9's in the dash (4 ways). Originally I was going to put them behind the seats somewhere, but from what people are saying this seems to just make the music loud not clear.<P>Would it make more sense to put the 6x9's in the doors and the 6"1/2's in the dash?<P>Basically, What is the best way to position these speakers?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||10-22-2001||06:56 PM||||If it were me, I'd sell the 6x9s and buy a sub.  Put both the 6 1/2" mids and the tweeters in the doors and the sub just about anywhere.  Maybe an amp and you're all set.  That would basically be my setup except I'm using 5 1/4" components.  Sounds great.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||10-22-2001||07:33 PM||||Yeah, I agree. Put your 6.5" in the doors, or kickpanels, like AusFieros setup, and ditch the dash speakers. Escentially you want the speakers aimed at your ears, more so for the higher freq. speakers. Bass is omni-directional, so it doesn't matter, but midbass, midrange, and high's should be aimed. ||||reg||1
